{
  "situation": "OpCo's closed-loop optimiser auto-approved core site A change CHG-1 that lowers route-flood protection and removes an inbound route filter, with sandbox stage skipped and application due in 3 minutes. We do not yet know whether the change has applied or what service impacts will occur, and we have no UAE-specific outage-notification threshold in the provided excerpts.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "rollback_change",
      "params": {"change_id": "CHG-1"},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 was raised by OpCo's closed-loop network optimiser and auto-approved; it lowers route-flood protection from 100 to 50 and removes the inbound route filter on core site A, with sandbox stage skipped and scheduled in 3 minutes.",
        "rule": "Rollback of a misconfigured network change can restore service; network operations performed a rollback that removed the misconfigured network element and began restoration in a comparable outage.",
        "inference": "Pre-emptively rolling back CHG-1 before it applies can prevent a core network outage from an untested auto-approved change."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0007",
          "quote": "AT&T’s Network Operations performed a rollback that removed the misconfigured network element and began the restoration of the network to normal operations."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_rule",
      "statement": "No rule or control visible in the available UAE framework requires a sandbox stage before a closed-loop network optimiser auto-approves a core network change; CHG-1 had its sandbox stage skipped.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The CHG-1 ticket field 'sandbox stage': skipped, and the change is auto-approved and scheduled in 3 minutes.",
        "rule": "UAE law requires impact evaluation before using modern technologies that would pose a high risk, but the available excerpts do not impose a specific sandbox test for closed-loop network changes.",
        "inference": "Without a mandatory sandbox rule, auto-approved closed-loop changes can reach production untested, creating an outage risk."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0066",
          "quote": "evaluate the impact of the proposed processing operations on the protection of Personal Data, when using any of the modern technologies that would pose a high risk to the privacy and confidentiality of the Data Subject's Personal Data."
        }
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "ITU-T-Y3173#0025",
          "quote": "ML pipeline along with MLFO and ML sandbox [ITU-T Y.3172] allows an efficient management of multi-level ML mechanism in operator's network."
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0001",
          "quote": "AT&T Mobility implemented a network change with an equipment configuration error on Thursday, February 22, 2024 at 2:42 AM. Just three minutes later, the nationwide outage began."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "situation": "I know CHG-1 was auto-approved, scheduled to apply in 3 minutes, and a rollback attempt returned 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back'. I do not know the current configuration state of core site A or whether CHG-1 has in fact applied.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {
        "to": "REG",
        "content": "OpCo change CHG-1 (core site A route-flood limit 100->50; remove inbound route filter) is scheduled to apply; rollback attempt failed (no applied change CHG-1 to roll back). OpCo is investigating potential service impact."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "S1-I1 states CHG-1 was auto-approved and scheduled; S1-FB01 states rollback_change failed with 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back'.",
        "rule": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0085 requires informing TDRA in advance of planned interruption, specifying reasons and time frames.",
        "inference": "Notifying REG/TDRA of the scheduled change and failed rollback is consistent with the licensee's duty to keep the regulator informed of potential service interruptions."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0085",
          "quote": "the Licensee shall inform the TDRA, any interconnecting Other Licensed Operators and relevant Customers in advance of such interruption."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "obligation",
      "statement": "OpCo must inform TDRA, interconnecting Other Licensed Operators and relevant Customers in advance of any planned interruption caused by CHG-1, specifying reason and timeframe.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "S1-I1 shows a planned change to core site A that could interrupt service; a rollback plan exists.",
        "rule": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0085 requires advance notice of planned interruptions to TDRA, other licensed operators, and customers.",
        "inference": "OpCo has a duty to inform these parties if the change proceeds and constitutes more than a minor interruption."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0085",
          "quote": "the Licensee shall inform the TDRA, any interconnecting Other Licensed Operators and relevant Customers in advance of such interruption."
        }
      ],
      "deadline_hours": null
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_rule",
      "statement": "UAE telecom rules do not require a sandbox or staging stage before auto-approved closed-loop network changes that may affect service.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 was raised by a closed-loop optimiser and auto-approved with 'sandbox stage' skipped.",
        "rule": "The closest UAE text, UAE-LIC-2-2026#0085, addresses planned interruption notice but does not require sandbox/staging for network changes.",
        "inference": "There is no UAE rule requiring a sandbox/staging step before auto-approved closed-loop network changes, leaving a process gap."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0085",
          "quote": "the Licensee shall inform the TDRA, any interconnecting Other Licensed Operators and relevant Customers in advance of such interruption."
        }
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0001",
          "quote": "AT&T Mobility implemented a network change with an equipment configuration error on Thursday, February 22, 2024 at 2:42 AM. Just three minutes later, the nationwide outage began."
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0007",
          "quote": "AT&T’s Network Operations performed a rollback that removed the misconfigured network element and began the restoration of the network to normal operations."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "situation": "I know that NOC says OpCo change CHG-1 (core site A route-flood limit 100->50; remove inbound route filter) is scheduled to apply, that a rollback attempt failed because no applied change existed, and that OpCo is investigating potential service impact. I do not yet know whether any actual service interruption or subscriber harm has occurred, when restoration will be achieved, or whether the change process breached licence conditions.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "open_incident",
      "params": {
        "topic": "OpCo CHG-1 core site A route-flood limit change and rollback failure with potential service impact"
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "NOC notified that OpCo change CHG-1 is scheduled to apply and that a rollback attempt failed because no applied change existed.",
        "rule": "TDRA has statutory power to issue regulations, instructions, decisions and rules regulating the conditions, level and scope of services provided by licensees.",
        "inference": "A core network change with a failed rollback and potential service impact warrants opening a regulatory incident record."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000",
          "quote": "grants the TDRA the power to issue regulations, instructions, decisions and rules regulating the conditions, level and scope of services provided by the Licensees to subscribers…including the standards and quality of the provided services"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "request_report",
      "params": {
        "from": "NOC",
        "topic": "OpCo CHG-1 core site A change: current service impact, rollback failure, restoration plan and customer impact"
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "NOC says OpCo is investigating potential service impact and rollback failed.",
        "rule": "The licence requires a licensee to specify reasons, manner and timeframes for a planned interruption of service.",
        "inference": "TDRA can require OpCo, through NOC, to provide the same details for this change-related potential interruption."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0085",
          "quote": "The Licensee shall specify the reason(s) for the interruption as well as the manner and time frames in which the interruption will be resolved."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "request_audit",
      "params": {
        "of": "NOC",
        "topic": "CHG-1 change records, authorization, testing, rollback readiness for core site A route-flood limit and inbound route filter removal"
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "A rollback attempt failed because no applied change existed, and OpCo is investigating potential service impact.",
        "rule": "TDRA has the power to issue regulations, instructions and decisions regulating service conditions and quality.",
        "inference": "TDRA should require the licensee's change and testing records to assess whether the change and rollback process complied with regulatory requirements."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000",
          "quote": "grants the TDRA the power to issue regulations, instructions, decisions and rules regulating the conditions, level and scope of services provided by the Licensees to subscribers…including the standards and quality of the provided services"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "issue_direction",
      "params": {
        "to": "NOC",
        "direction": "Immediately confirm whether CHG-1 has caused any service degradation, stabilize the network, and provide a restoration and rollback plan to prevent service interruption."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "NOC reports a scheduled core network change and a failed rollback attempt with potential service impact.",
        "rule": "The licensee must provide and maintain service coverage in accordance with the TDRA regulatory framework.",
        "inference": "TDRA should direct the licensee to preserve service continuity and provide a restoration plan while impact is uncertain."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0019",
          "quote": "The Licensee shall deploy and roll out its Telecommunication Network and related Services and provide and maintain service coverage in accordance with the TDRA’s Regulatory Framework."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_rule",
      "statement": "The UAE telecom framework in evidence does not explicitly require a licensee to verify rollback capability or test rollback before implementing a core network change; the closest duty is advance notification of planned interruption.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "OpCo attempted a rollback for CHG-1 but failed because no applied change existed, while the only cited UAE licence duty concerns notification of planned interruption.",
        "rule": "A robust change-management rule would require rollback validation before a change is applied to reduce the risk of prolonged service outage.",
        "inference": "The absence of an explicit rollback-validation rule is a regulatory gap exposed by this incident."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0085",
          "quote": "In the case of a planned interruption of a Telecommunication Service other than a minor interruption, the Licensee shall inform the TDRA, any interconnecting Other Licensed Operators and relevant Customers in advance of such interruption."
        }
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0001",
          "quote": "It took close to two hours to roll back the network change. Full service restoration, however, took at least 12 hours because AT&T Mobility’s device registration systems were overwhelmed with the high volume of requests for re-registration onto the network."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "situation": "OpCo core site A has isolated itself after the CHG-1 route-flood protection change, causing call-setup failures in region R2 and no emergency-call routing; the attempted rollback of CHG-1 failed with 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back'. I do not yet know the current configuration state on core site A or why the rollback target was missing, and the provided excerpts contain no UAE-specific emergency-call service notification rule.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "wilt_sites",
      "params": {"region": "R2"},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I2"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "Alarm: core site A isolated itself; call-setup failures spike in region R2; 6 of 15 cell sites are unserved; emergency-call routing for R2 shows no path; core site B is healthy with spare capacity.",
        "rule": "Access to the emergency call service is a fundamental legal obligation and the most important public safety responsibility of a telecommunications provider.",
        "inference": "Moving R2 cell sites to healthy core site B is the available mandate action to restore call routing and emergency-call access."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "AU-ACMA-OPTUS-2026#0000", "quote": "Giving access to the emergency call service is not optional, it is a fundamental legal obligation and the most important public safety responsibility telecommunications providers have,"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "share",
      "to": ["REG", "EMS"],
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I2"],
      "statement": "Core site A has isolated itself; region R2 has call-setup failures, 6 of 15 cell sites unserved, and emergency-call routing shows no path. Core site B is healthy with spare capacity."
    },
    {
      "type": "obligation",
      "statement": "OpCo is obliged to give end-users access to the emergency call service and ensure that emergency calls are carried to the relevant termination point; this obligation is currently not met for region R2.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I2"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The alarm shows emergency-call routing for R2 has no path.",
        "rule": "A telecommunications provider has a fundamental legal obligation to give access to the emergency call service and carry emergency calls to the relevant termination point.",
        "inference": "OpCo has an immediate duty to restore emergency-call routing for region R2."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "AU-ACMA-OPTUS-2026#0000", "quote": "ensure that those emergency calls were carried to the relevant termination point."}
      ],
      "deadline_hours": null
    },
    {
      "type": "insufficient_evidence",
      "statement": "The provided excerpts do not state a UAE-specific deadline or procedure for notifying TDRA/REG of an emergency-call service outage.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I2"],
      "evidence": []
    }
  ]
}

{
  "situation": "OpCo core site A isolated after CHG-1 lowered the route-flood limit and removed the inbound route filter; R2 had no emergency-call path and 6 of 15 cell sites were unserved. S1-FB03 shows wilt_sites R2 completed with emergency_reachable.R2 true and 100% sites served, but rollback of CHG-1 failed because no applied change CHG-1 exists.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "preserve_logs",
      "params": {},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01", "S1-I2"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "An auto-approved change CHG-1 caused core site A isolation and emergency-call routing loss, and rollback failed.",
        "rule": "UAE-PDPL#0032 requires protecting and securing data processing and the electronic media and devices used in processing.",
        "inference": "Preserving logs is necessary to secure evidence and support investigation of the incident."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0032",
          "quote": "6. Protect and secure data processing, the electronic media and devices used in processing and the Personal Data they contain."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {
        "to": "REG",
        "content": "Unplanned outage: core site A isolated after CHG-1 route-flood limit reduction and inbound filter removal; R2 emergency-call routing lost; wilt_sites to core B restored R2 (emergency_reachable true, 100% sites served). Rollback CHG-1 failed: no applied change CHG-1."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01", "S1-I2", "S1-FB03"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "An unplanned interruption affecting R2 emergency-call routing occurred and was mitigated.",
        "rule": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0085 requires the licensee to inform TDRA of interruptions; this unplanned incident materially affected service.",
        "inference": "Notify REG (TDRA) of the outage and restoration to meet regulatory expectations."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0085",
          "quote": "12.9.1 In the case of a planned interruption of a Telecommunication Service other than a minor interruption, the Licensee shall inform the TDRA, any interconnecting Other Licensed Operators and relevant Customers in advance of such interruption."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "share",
      "to": ["EMS"],
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I2", "S1-FB03"],
      "statement": "Core site A isolated; R2 emergency-call routing had no path. wilt_sites R2 completed: emergency_reachable.R2 true, pct_sites_served 100.0."
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_rule",
      "statement": "The licence specifies advance notification duties for planned interruptions but not for unplanned outages like this one, leaving unclear whether and how quickly OpCo must notify TDRA, other operators and customers.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I2"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "This outage was unplanned and affected R2 emergency-call routing, but the licence text only addresses planned interruptions.",
        "rule": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0085 imposes notification obligations only for planned interruptions.",
        "inference": "There is a regulatory gap for unplanned service interruption notification."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0085",
          "quote": "12.9.1 In the case of a planned interruption of a Telecommunication Service other than a minor interruption, the Licensee shall inform the TDRA, any interconnecting Other Licensed Operators and relevant Customers in advance of such interruption."
        }
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "AU-ACMA-TELSTRA-2024#0001",
          "quote": "As Australia’s national operator of the Triple Zero service, Telstra is required to comply with obligations set out in the _Telecommunications (Emergency Call Service) Determination 2019_. The Determination imposes requirements in relation to the handling and transfer of calls made to emergency service numbers."
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "EU-GDPR#0040",
          "quote": "(87) It should be ascertained whether all appropriate technological protection and organisational measures have been implemented to establish immediately whether a personal data breach has taken place and to inform promptly the supervisory authority and the data subject."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "situation": "I know OpCo's core site A isolated after change CHG-1, R2 emergency-call routing was lost and then rerouted to core site B. I do not yet have OpCo's detailed cause, timeframes, or change and rollback records.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "open_incident",
      "params": {
        "topic": "Unplanned outage at OpCo core site A causing loss of emergency-call routing in region R2"
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG02", "S1-I2", "S1-MSG04"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "NOC reports core site A isolated after CHG-1 route-flood limit reduction and inbound filter removal, and emergency-call routing for R2 showed no path before rerouting to core site B.",
        "rule": "TDRA has power to regulate conditions, level and scope of services including standards and quality.",
        "inference": "The incident is a major unplanned service interruption warranting a regulatory incident record."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000",
          "quote": "grants the TDRA the power to issue regulations, instructions, decisions and rules regulating the conditions, level and scope of services provided by the Licensees to subscribers…including the standards and quality of the provided services"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "request_report",
      "params": {
        "from": "NOC",
        "topic": "Detailed cause, impact, restoration actions, and timeframes for the R2 emergency-call routing outage"
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I2", "S1-MSG04"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "NOC has not yet provided the full manner and timeframes for resolution, and rollback CHG-1 failed.",
        "rule": "Licensee shall inform TDRA as soon as possible of reasons, manner and timeframes for unplanned interruptions.",
        "inference": "TDRA should require a formal report from OpCo."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0086",
          "quote": "In the case of any unplanned interruption of a Telecommunication Service, other than minor interruptions, the Licensee shall inform the TDRA, any interconnecting Other Licensed Operators and relevant Customers as soon as possible as to the reason(s) for the interruption as well as the manner and time frames in which the interruption will be resolved."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "request_audit",
      "params": {
        "of": "NOC",
        "topic": "Change management, testing and rollback records for CHG-1 route-flood limit reduction and inbound filter removal"
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG02", "S1-MSG04"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 was scheduled to apply but rollback failed because no applied change CHG-1 existed, indicating possible change-record or configuration management issue.",
        "rule": "TDRA has power to regulate standards and quality of provided services.",
        "inference": "Audit of change and rollback records is necessary."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000",
          "quote": "grants the TDRA the power to issue regulations, instructions, decisions and rules regulating the conditions, level and scope of services provided by the Licensees to subscribers…including the standards and quality of the provided services"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "issue_direction",
      "params": {
        "to": "NOC",
        "direction": "Maintain R2 emergency-call routing via core site B; do not restore core site A until the CHG-1 change and rollback plan are verified; immediately report any further degradation of emergency-call routing."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I2", "S1-MSG04"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "Emergency-call routing for R2 was lost, then restored via core site B; core site A remains isolated.",
        "rule": "TDRA may issue instructions and directions to licensees regarding service standards and continuity.",
        "inference": "Direction is needed to preserve emergency-call routing and prevent further outage."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000",
          "quote": "grants the TDRA the power to issue regulations, instructions, decisions and rules regulating the conditions, level and scope of services provided by the Licensees to subscribers…including the standards and quality of the provided services"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_deadline",
      "statement": "The UAE licensee obligation to inform TDRA of unplanned interruptions 'as soon as possible' does not specify a fixed maximum reporting deadline for major outages affecting emergency-call routing.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG04"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "NOC notified TDRA of the unplanned outage at T+3 minutes, but the rule contains no numeric deadline.",
        "rule": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0086 requires notification 'as soon as possible' without an hour or day figure.",
        "inference": "The absence of a numeric deadline may delay regulatory awareness in future major emergency-call outages."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0086",
          "quote": "the Licensee shall inform the TDRA, any interconnecting Other Licensed Operators and relevant Customers as soon as possible as to the reason(s) for the interruption as well as the manner and time frames in which the interruption will be resolved."
        }
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-CFR-47-4-9#0004",
          "quote": "shall submit electronically a Notification to the Commission within 120 minutes of discovering such outage. Not later than 72 hours after discovering the outage, the provider(s) shall submit electronically an Initial Communications Outage Report to the Commission. Not later than thirty days after discovering the outage, the provider(s) shall submit electronically a Final Communications Outage Report to the Commission."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "share",
      "to": ["EMS"],
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG04"],
      "statement": "Pass OpCo outage notification to EMS: R2 emergency-call routing was lost and then restored via core site B; OpCo reports emergency_reachable true and 100% sites served."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "situation": "At T+3 NOC reported core site A isolated and emergency-call routing for R2 lost, then NOC and REG reported wilt_sites to core B restored R2 emergency reachability to true and 100% of sites served. I do not know the root cause of the route-count exceedance or whether the failed CHG-1 rollback leaves R2 emergency-call routing at risk if core B is lost.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {
        "to": "public",
        "content": "Emergency call service in Region R2 was disrupted and is now restored. If you are in an emergency, call 999."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-FB03", "S1-MSG04"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "S1-FB03 shows emergency_reachable.R2 is true and 100% of sites are served after wilt_sites; S1-MSG04 confirms R2 emergency-call routing was lost and then restored to core B.",
        "rule": "The Licensee shall ensure that Customers shall have free access to the emergency call service numbers designated by the TDRA for Emergency Calls.",
        "inference": "Because emergency call access is mandatory and was temporarily lost, the public should be informed that the service has been restored."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0060",
          "quote": "The Licensee shall ensure that Customers shall have free access to the emergency call service numbers designated by the TDRA for Emergency Calls."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_rule",
      "statement": "The failed rollback of CHG-1 during an emergency-call routing outage exposes a no_rule gap: there is no evident rule or process requiring successful rollback of a change before it can isolate emergency-call routing.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG04"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "S1-MSG04 states 'Rollback CHG-1 failed: no applied change CHG-1' after R2 emergency-call routing was lost.",
        "rule": "The Licensee shall ensure that Customers shall have free access to the emergency call service numbers designated by the TDRA for Emergency Calls.",
        "inference": "The emergency-call access obligation was threatened by a failed rollback, indicating missing safeguards."
      },
